PLACEHOLDER — CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH

This file was added by the F-25 remediation to close the "no LICENSE" gap on
a PUBLIC repository, where the absence of a licence leaves the terms of use
ambiguous. Proprietary / all-rights-reserved is the conservative default: it
preserves every option, including later relicensing under open-source terms.

Choosing a licence is a business decision, not an engineering one. Confirm
with the copyright holder, and have counsel review alongside the Terms and
Privacy Policy required by audit finding F-07. If Mekholi is intended to be
open source, replace this file entirely — do not amend it.

Note also that this repository is currently PUBLIC. The database schema, RLS
policies, and RPC definitions are therefore world-readable. That is defensible
(the security model does not depend on secrecy), but it must be deliberate,
and it means any credential ever committed is public the instant it lands.
